      "body": "Reopened from #40675. GitHub closed that PR on 2 October when the fork it came from was deleted; its review history is still there.\n\nMiMo omits `packed_modules_mapping`, so ModelOpt mixed-precision policies for separate checkpoint projections do not reach their fused runtime layers. With NVFP4 experts and block-FP8 dense layers, loading fails at `model.layers.0.mlp.gate_up_proj.weight_scale_inv` because the fused layer never receives its FP8 policy.\n\nDeclare the gate/up and split-QKV mappings. The new CPU tests exercise the actual ModelOpt resolver: retained block-FP8 gate/up, split and already-fused QKV, rejection of conflicting fused policies, and an unquantized output projection.\n\nValidation: all five tests pass remotely. Applying the model metadata mapping to SGLang 0f6761b54 also allows the full MiMo-V2.6-Flash-RL NVFP4 checkpoint to load and generate on four RTX PRO 6000 Blackwell cards (TP4/EP4, FlashInfer CUTLASS, Triton attention). An eight-turn conversation returned the expected answers and reused the complete preceding prefix on every later turn. No kernel or activation-precision changes are included.\n\nDuplicate check on 2026-09-22: clean application to upstream b44e2486824e; inspected #37261 and #39080 (DeepEP-v2 dispatch) and #39885 (pipeline/MTP handling). Their MiMo changes do not declare these quantization mappings.\n\n## Rebase validation (2026-10-02)\n\nRebased onto upstream `f2385314b2b3` on 2026-10-04; the two commits are patch-identical to the 2026-10-02 revision. All 5 policy tests pass. The repo's pre-commit hooks pass on the changed files.\n\nChanged Python files pass isort, Ruff lint/format and codespell; the diff passes whitespace checks. Earlier hardware and whole-model measurements above predate this rebase and were not rerun. Upstream test workflows still require a maintainer to add `run-ci`.\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #37171296210](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/37171296210)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #37171296095](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/37171296095)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #37171296145](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/37171296145)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
